### Sample HTML/CSS/JavaScript Code for an Ad

This snippet includes a typical ad configuration you might find integrating Google AdSense on a healthcare website:

```html
<div class="ad-banner" id="health-special-offer" data-ad-id="98765" data-campaign="wellness-ad">
 <style>
 .ad-banner {
 width: 300px;
 height: 250px;
 margin: auto;
 border: 1px solid #ccc;
 background-color: #f9f9f9;
 position: relative;
 }
 .ad-content {
 text-align: center;
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 padding: 20px;
 }
 .cta-button {
 display: inline-block;
 margin-top: 10px;
 padding: 10px 15px;
 background-color: #007bff;
 color: #fff;
 text-decoration: none;
 border-radius: 5px;
 transition: background-color 0.3s;
 }
 .cta-button:hover {
 background-color: #0056b3;
 }
 </style>

 <div class="ad-content">
 <h3>Special Wellness Offer!</h3>
 <img src="wellness_offer.jpg" alt="Wellness Offer" width="280" height="150">
 <a href="#" class="cta-button">Learn More</a>
 </div>

 <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script>
 <ins class="adsbygoogle"
 style="display:block"
 data-ad-client="ca-pub-456789"
 data-ad-slot="67890"
 data-ad-format="auto">
 </ins>

 <script>
 document.querySelector('.cta-button').addEventListener('click', function(event) {
 console.log('Ad Clicked: Special Wellness Offer');
 // Additional tracking logic here
 });
 (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
 </script>
</div>
```
**Classification: is_ad: true** 
**Ad Type: banner**

--- 

### Explanation:
- **Ad Integration:** The `<script>` tag, along with `<ins class="adsbygoogle">`, is an indicator of Google AdSense.
- **Tracking & Events:** The `addEventListener` for the `click` event on the `.cta-button` logs a message whenever someone interacts with the button, indicating tracking behavior.
- **Promotional Content:** Typical promotional assets like special offer images and CTAs such as "Learn More" are present.

